              "id": "CVE-2026-54518",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-54518 Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in pkg:maven\/com.fasterxml.jackson.core\/jackson-databind@2.21.2"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "jackson-databind contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor. From 2.21.0 until 2.21.4 and 3.1.4, UnwrappedPropertyHandler.processUnwrappedCreatorProperties() replays buffered JSON into creator parameters but never consults prop.visibleInView(activeView). The normal property-based creator path gates creator properties on the active view, but this unwrapped-creator replay path bypasses that check, so a constructor parameter annotated with both @JsonView(AdminView.class) and @JsonUnwrapped is populated from attacker JSON even when a more restrictive view is active. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.21.4 and 3.1.4."
              },
              "help": {
