                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-49459 Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify is a DOM-only cross-site scripting sanitizer for HTML, MathML, and SVG. Prior to 3.4.6, DOMPurify.sanitize(root, { IN_PLACE: true }) could preserve event-handler attributes on an attacker-controlled <form> root when a descendant name clobbered properties checked by _isClobbered, because _forceRemove no-opped on the parent-less root and _sanitizeAttributes returned early. This issue is fixed in version 3.4.6."
