              "id": "CVE-2026-41239",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-41239 vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify's SAFE_FOR_TEMPLATES feature fails to strip Mustache\/template expressions when RETURN_DOM or RETURN_DOM_FRAGMENT is used. The final string-scrubbing pass that removes expressions like {{...}} is skipped in DOM-return mode, and split text nodes (e.g. from removed intermediate tags) can rejoin to form a complete expression that template-evaluating frameworks like Vue 2 will execute."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file.\nFor more information see [How dependency-check works](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html),\n[How to read the HTML report](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and\n[Suppressing false positives](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "source": "RETIREJS"
              }
            },{
              "id": "CVE-2026-41238",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-41238 vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify versions 3.0.1 through 3.3.3 are vulnerable to an XSS bypass via prototype pollution. When no CUSTOM_ELEMENT_HANDLING is specified, the fallback plain object inherits from Object.prototype; if an attacker has polluted Object.prototype.tagNameCheck and Object.prototype.attributeNameCheck with permissive regexes, DOMPurify allows arbitrary custom elements with event handler attributes through sanitization."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file.\nFor more information see [How dependency-check works](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html),\n[How to read the HTML report](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and\n[Suppressing false positives](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "source": "RETIREJS"
              }
            },{
              "id": "CVE-2026-65901",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "low severity - CVE-2026-65901 vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify: `IN_PLACE` mode trusts attacker-controlled `nodeName` on live non-form nodes, allowing script retention and XSS via attacker-supplied DOM objects"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file.\nFor more information see [How dependency-check works](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html),\n[How to read the HTML report](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and\n[Suppressing false positives](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "source": "RETIREJS"
              }
            },{
              "id": "CVE-2026-65900",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "low severity - CVE-2026-65900 vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify: SAFE_FOR_TEMPLATES bypass - template expressions survive sanitization inside <template> content when using DOM output modes"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file.\nFor more information see [How dependency-check works](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html),\n[How to read the HTML report](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and\n[Suppressing false positives](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "source": "RETIREJS"
              }
            },{
              "id": "CVE-2026-65903",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-65903 vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify has a logic inconsistency where FORBID_TAGS is not checked when a function-based ADD_TAGS (tagCheck) returns true. Due to short-circuit evaluation, the FORBID_TAGS check is never evaluated, allowing explicitly forbidden elements to pass through sanitization when EXTRA_ELEMENT_HANDLING.tagCheck is configured."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file.\nFor more information see [How dependency-check works](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html),\n[How to read the HTML report](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and\n[Suppressing false positives](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "source": "RETIREJS"
              }
            },{
              "id": "CVE-2026-65902",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-65902 vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify: Hook mutation of `data.allowedTags` \/ `data.allowedAttributes` permanently pollutes `DEFAULT_ALLOWED_TAGS` \/ `DEFAULT_ALLOWED_ATTR`"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file.\nFor more information see [How dependency-check works](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html),\n[How to read the HTML report](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and\n[Suppressing false positives](https://dependency-check.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."
